{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X12XXijeDbBUBzEQHrWqkA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R79 — Contract gate — Extension ↔ Daemon review-UI MCP plumbing\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** Contract gate after Phase 10\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** R64, R78\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface), [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§MCP Tool Contract Principles](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles)\n8\t**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Purpose\n11\t\n12\tThis review is the contract gate between the Phase 10 review UI and the daemon MCP surface that powers it. Every method on `ReviewRpcBridge` calls a tool registered on the daemon side; this gate verifies that every method has a matching tool, that the JSON shapes round-trip end to end, that the schema is documented and regression-tested, and that no surface added by Phases 6–9 was forgotten on the extension side. The gate exists because UI compile + lint cannot detect contract drift — only an integration test that sends a real request to a real daemon and asserts the response shape can. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties demands \"every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested\"; this review enforces that for the review UI surface.\n13\t\n14\t## Inputs to read\n15\t\n16\t- Every artifact produced by T71–T77 (extension review surface).\n17\t- Every artifact produced by Phase 6–9 MCP work the review UI depends on, including the R64 contract gate output for the MCP tool schema.\n18\t- Existing files this review cross-checks:\n19\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — registered MCP tools.\n20\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server.\n21\t  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed extension-side bridge.\n22\t  - `extension/src/daemon.ts` — underlying JSON-RPC client.\n23\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (from T02) — backward-compatibility policy this gate enforces.\n24\t- Spec sections: `## 9. MCP Surface`, `## 10. Human Review Surface`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`.\n25\t- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (schema parity, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward-compatibility discipline).\n26\t\n27\t## Review procedure\n28\t\n29\t1. Enumerate every method exposed by `ReviewRpcBridge` and confirm each maps to a registered MCP tool in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`. Any orphan method on either side is a blocker.\n30\t2. For every mapped pair, inspect the typed request and response shapes on the TypeScript side (`rpcBridge.ts`) and the corresponding Rust schema in `mcp.rs` (and its serde structs). Field-by-field comparison: type, required/optional, name. Drift is a blocker per `coding.md` §Schema parity.\n31\t3. Cross-check `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) — every review-UI tool is either `stable`, `additive`, or `redesigned-with-shim`; nothing is undocumented.\n32\t4. Create `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` (this is the deliverable contract test). The test launches a real daemon process via the existing pattern in `extension/src/test/`, sends one round-trip request per review-UI bridge method, and asserts the response parses into the typed shape. Include happy-path requests and an error-path request per tool. Tests use the real daemon binary (`daemon/target/release/lattice`), not a mock.\n33\t5. Run the contract suite with `cd extension && npm install && npm run compile && npm test`. Confirm every round-trip passes. If the daemon binary is not present in `extension/bin/`, the test setup builds and copies per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy: `cd daemon && cargo build --release && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/`.\n34\t6. Confirm the contract test exercises every review-UI tool from `rpcBridge.ts`: memory listing, evidence inspection, promotion queue read + apply + reject, contradiction queue read + apply + reject, stale listing, verify_memory, event trace read, retrieval explanation read, consolidation queue read + retry, indexing health read, graph health read + recompute.\n35\t7. Grep `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` for the corresponding tool registrations and confirm each accepts the documented request shape and returns the documented response shape.\n36\t8. Cross-check that backward-compat shims from R64 (if any) are still in place: every legacy tool name continues to route to the new implementation.\n37\t\n38\t## Required sections in the review output file\n39\t\n40\tThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n41\t\n42\t- `## Contract surfaces` — table of every `ReviewRpcBridge` method, the corresponding daemon tool name, the request shape, the response shape, and the spec citation. One row per method.\n43\t- `## Round-trip evidence` — for every method, the contract-test name in `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` that exercises it; the test output snippet showing the request, the response, and the assertion that the typed shape parsed; the daemon log line showing the request was received.\n44\t- `## Schema surfaces` — TypeScript ↔ Rust field comparison table per tool. Columns: TS field, TS type, TS required, Rust field, Rust type, Rust required, parity verdict. Any drift is flagged.\n45\t- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n46\t- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n47\t\n48\t## Verification\n49\t\n50\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream tasks can read it.\n51\t- `test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` — confirms the new contract test file exists.\n52\t- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms contract surfaces enumerated under a dedicated heading.\n53\t- `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms round-trip evidence is present.\n54\t- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile (including the new contract test) succeeds.\n55\t- `cd extension && npm test` — the contract suite plus all prior tests pass against a real daemon.\n56\t\n57\t## Definition of done\n58\t\n59\t- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n60\t- [ ] `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` exists, compiles, and passes against the real daemon binary.\n61\t- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n62\t- [ ] `## Schema surfaces` and `## Findings` are also present (not gated by tasks.json verification but required for completeness).\n63\t- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbec9507-2ec8-4c28-a044-dba0cf5769ae","uuid":"0627d8cd-5aa3-46a1-bf78-bb985ea5db4d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:05:55.646Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R79.md","content":"# R79 — Contract gate — Extension ↔ Daemon review-UI MCP plumbing\n\n**Phase:** Contract gate after Phase 10\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R64, R78\n**Spec anchor:** [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface), [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§MCP Tool Contract Principles](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review is the contract gate between the Phase 10 review UI and the daemon MCP surface that powers it. Every method on `ReviewRpcBridge` calls a tool registered on the daemon side; this gate verifies that every method has a matching tool, that the JSON shapes round-trip end to end, that the schema is documented and regression-tested, and that no surface added by Phases 6–9 was forgotten on the extension side. The gate exists because UI compile + lint cannot detect contract drift — only an integration test that sends a real request to a real daemon and asserts the response shape can. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties demands \"every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested\"; this review enforces that for the review UI surface.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by T71–T77 (extension review surface).\n- Every artifact produced by Phase 6–9 MCP work the review UI depends on, including the R64 contract gate output for the MCP tool schema.\n- Existing files this review cross-checks:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — registered MCP tools.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server.\n  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed extension-side bridge.\n  - `extension/src/daemon.ts` — underlying JSON-RPC client.\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (from T02) — backward-compatibility policy this gate enforces.\n- Spec sections: `## 9. MCP Surface`, `## 10. Human Review Surface`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`.\n- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (schema parity, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward-compatibility discipline).\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Enumerate every method exposed by `ReviewRpcBridge` and confirm each maps to a registered MCP tool in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`. Any orphan method on either side is a blocker.\n2. For every mapped pair, inspect the typed request and response shapes on the TypeScript side (`rpcBridge.ts`) and the corresponding Rust schema in `mcp.rs` (and its serde structs). Field-by-field comparison: type, required/optional, name. Drift is a blocker per `coding.md` §Schema parity.\n3. Cross-check `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) — every review-UI tool is either `stable`, `additive`, or `redesigned-with-shim`; nothing is undocumented.\n4. Create `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` (this is the deliverable contract test). The test launches a real daemon process via the existing pattern in `extension/src/test/`, sends one round-trip request per review-UI bridge method, and asserts the response parses into the typed shape. Include happy-path requests and an error-path request per tool. Tests use the real daemon binary (`daemon/target/release/lattice`), not a mock.\n5. Run the contract suite with `cd extension && npm install && npm run compile && npm test`. Confirm every round-trip passes. If the daemon binary is not present in `extension/bin/`, the test setup builds and copies per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy: `cd daemon && cargo build --release && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/`.\n6. Confirm the contract test exercises every review-UI tool from `rpcBridge.ts`: memory listing, evidence inspection, promotion queue read + apply + reject, contradiction queue read + apply + reject, stale listing, verify_memory, event trace read, retrieval explanation read, consolidation queue read + retry, indexing health read, graph health read + recompute.\n7. Grep `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` for the corresponding tool registrations and confirm each accepts the documented request shape and returns the documented response shape.\n8. Cross-check that backward-compat shims from R64 (if any) are still in place: every legacy tool name continues to route to the new implementation.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Contract surfaces` — table of every `ReviewRpcBridge` method, the corresponding daemon tool name, the request shape, the response shape, and the spec citation. One row per method.\n- `## Round-trip evidence` — for every method, the contract-test name in `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` that exercises it; the test output snippet showing the request, the response, and the assertion that the typed shape parsed; the daemon log line showing the request was received.\n- `## Schema surfaces` — TypeScript ↔ Rust field comparison table per tool. Columns: TS field, TS type, TS required, Rust field, Rust type, Rust required, parity verdict. Any drift is flagged.\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream tasks can read it.\n- `test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` — confirms the new contract test file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms contract surfaces enumerated under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms round-trip evidence is present.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile (including the new contract test) succeeds.\n- `cd extension && npm test` — the contract suite plus all prior tests pass against a real daemon.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` exists, compiles, and passes against the real daemon binary.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] `## Schema surfaces` and `## Findings` are also present (not gated by tasks.json verification but required for completeness).\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}}}
