{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Yb8V84bM58LSF7nVqMfWHC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R64 — Phase 8 MCP tool surface schema regression (contract gate)\n2\t\n3\t> \"Every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested.\"\n4\t> — [`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md) `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`.\n5\t\n6\tThis contract gate covers the redesigned MCP tool surface delivered in Phase 8 (T56–T62). It binds the daemon implementation in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs::handle_tools_list` / `handle_tools_call` to the canonical reference in [`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md`](../../../architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md) `## Final tool list`, and to the compatibility rules in [`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`](../../../architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md) `## Backward compatibility` / `## Shim removal protocol`.\n7\t\n8\tThe regression test file is `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_schema_tests.rs`, split into the submodules `tool_list.rs`, `round_trip.rs`, `render_modes.rs`, `shims.rs`, and `backward_compat.rs` to stay within the 800-line ceiling from the Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`.\n9\t\n10\tSpec excerpts that bind this gate verbatim:\n11\t\n12\t> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, diagnostic explanations where useful.\" — spec [`## MCP Surface`](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface).\n13\t\n14\t> \"Every assistant-facing tool should return: overview, ranked pivots, relevant context, memory highlights, event episodes where relevant, suggested next expansion, stable handles, risks or uncertainty, compact/full render choice, structured payload.\" — spec [`## MCP Tool Contract Principles`](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles).\n15\t\n16\t## Schema surfaces\n17\t\n18\tEvery tool advertised by `handle_tools_list` matches the canonical reference, and every advertised tool has at least one regression test in `mcp_schema_tests`. The check is enforced by `mcp_schema_tests::tool_list::advertised_tool_list_matches_the_reference_exactly`, which compares the names returned by `tools/list` against `ADVERTISED_TOOLS` (the 49-entry list lifted verbatim from `2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md ## Final tool list`).\n19\t\n20\t| # | Tool | `mcp.rs` definition | Reference row | `mcp_schema_tests` coverage |\n21\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n22\t| 1 | `get_context_capsule` | `mcp.rs:344–369` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:13` | `tool_list`, `shims::query_context_alias_dispatches_to_get_context_capsule` |\n23\t| 2 | `prepare_change` | `mcp.rs:369–419` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:14` | `tool_list` |\n24\t| 3 | `plan_edit` | `mcp.rs:419–470` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:15` | `tool_list` |\n25\t| 4 | `trace_scenario` | `mcp.rs:1456` (dispatch) | `mcp-tool-reference.md:16` | `tool_list` |\n26\t| 5 | `find_relevant_tests` | `mcp.rs:1457` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:17` | `tool_list` |\n27\t| 6 | `impact_from_diff` | `mcp.rs:1458` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:18` | `tool_list` |\n28\t| 7 | `get_working_set_context` | `mcp.rs:1459` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:19` | `tool_list` |\n29\t| 8 | `summarize_subsystem` | `mcp.rs:1460` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:20` | `tool_list` |\n30\t| 9 | `get_repo_playbook` | `mcp.rs:1461` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:21` | `tool_list` |\n31\t| 10 | `get_docs_capsule` | `mcp.rs:1462` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:22` | `tool_list` |\n32\t| 11 | `get_backlinks` | `mcp.rs:1463` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:23` | `tool_list` |\n33\t| 12 | `get_outgoing_links` | `mcp.rs:1464` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:24` | `tool_list` |\n34\t| 13 | `find_stale_docs` | `mcp.rs:1465` | `mcp-tool-reference.md:25` | `tool_list` |\n35\t| 14 | `diagnose_failure` | `mcp.rs:1466` | `mcp-tool-ref