{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Jp9TxrUventmamp9kCyDSz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Xxnz67PcTnf9Zy5jfYQyQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/R79.md","content":"# R79 — Result\n\n## Files created / modified\n\n- **Created (final):** `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — the full contract-gate review markdown with all required headings (`## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Schema surfaces`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`).\n- **Created (already-staged):** `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` — 20-test contract suite that spawns the real release-built daemon binary, exercises every review-UI MCP tool, and asserts every typed response parses through the same `normalize*` helpers the review panel consumes.\n- **Synchronized:** `extension/bin/lattice` rebuilt from `daemon/target/release/lattice` (md5 `0023b5e15e264d1383aa525784a2d6c9`) per `lattice/CLAUDE.md ## Deploy` so the contract test runs against the current daemon source state.\n- **No other source edits.** The bridge (`extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts`), the typed payload helpers (`extension/src/review/rpcPayloads.ts`), and the daemon-side dispatch (`daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`) were inspected; no schema drift required a fix.\n\n## Verification commands and outputs\n\nAll commands run from the repository root.\n\n| Command | Result | Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Schema surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Findings' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `cd extension && npm run compile` | pass | `tsc -p ./` exits 0, no diagnostics |\n| `cd extension && npm test` | pass | `Exit code: 0` (VS Code Test Electron harness) |\n\n### Direct mocha invocation of contract tests (highest-fidelity evidence)\n\n```\n$ cd extension && node -e \"\n  const Mocha = require('mocha');\n  const m = new Mocha({ ui: 'tdd', reporter: 'spec', timeout: 120_000 });\n  m.addFile('./out/test/contract.test.js');\n  m.run(failures => process.exit(failures > 0 ? 1 : 0));\n\"\n\n  contract: ReviewRpcBridge ↔ daemon MCP tools\n    ✔ list_observations: happy-path returns typed memory list\n    ✔ list_observations: invalid limit shape is gracefully clamped\n    ✔ list_stale_memories: happy-path returns typed memory list\n    ✔ list_stale_memories: oversize limit is clamped to ≤200\n    ✔ index_status: happy-path returns typed snapshot\n    ✔ get_session_metrics: happy-path returns typed session metrics\n    ✔ get_memory_metrics: happy-path returns typed metric snapshot\n    ✔ get_memory_metrics: invalid scope rejected by serde\n    ✔ get_event_trace: happy-path returns typed paginated page\n    ✔ get_event_trace: missing scope is rejected\n    ✔ consolidate_session: happy-path returns typed consolidation report\n    ✔ consolidate_session: empty session_id is rejected\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=propose returns typed proposal\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=reject closes the proposal\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=apply requires proposal_id\n    ✔ verify_explain_memory: happy-path returns typed verify-explain response (48ms)\n    ✔ verify_explain_memory: unknown memory id is rejected\n    ✔ list_memory_conflicts: happy-path on legacy anchor returns typed list\n    ✔ list_memory_conflicts: missing anchor is rejected\n    ✔ contract transcript captures every covered tool\n\n  20 passing (639ms)\n$ echo \"RC=$?\"\nRC=0\n```\n\nThis invocation runs against the real daemon binary `extension/bin/lattice` (no mocks, no fixtures), spawned per test suite via `cp.spawn(binaryPath, ['--stdio', '--workspace', workspace])` from `contract.test.ts:82–89`. Every test exercises a real `tools/call` and parses the response through the production `normalize*` helpers in `extension/src/review/rpcPayloads.ts`.\n\n### Files expected (per `tasks.json` `verification_commands` and `files_expected`)\n\n```\n$ test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md\n$ test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts\n$ echo \"both files exist\"\nboth files exist\n```\n\n## Issues encountered\n\n1. **`npm test` swallows inner mocha failures (pre-existing harness issue).** When the contract test runs through `@vscode/test-electron`, the runner reports `Exit code: 0` regardless of whether mocha tests inside the VS Code instance fail. Verified by inserting an intentional `assert.fail()` in a sanity test — the suite still reported exit 0. This is independent of R79's scope (it is a property of how the existing test harness propagates child exit codes). The contract test itself runs correctly and surfaces failures non-zero when invoked directly via `node ./out/test/contract.test.js`. Documented in the review under Findings #5; the verification commands `cd extension && npm run compile` and `cd extension && npm test` both pass as required by the task file, so the gate is satisfied. The high-fidelity evidence in the result above is the direct mocha invocation.\n2. **`e